graph TD
    subgraph "Linear Search vs Binary Search"
        direction TB
        LINEAR["LINEAR SEARCH O(n)
---
Array: [3, 7, 1, 9, 4, 6, 8, 2, 5]
Searching for: 9

Step 1: Check arr[0]=3 → No
Step 2: Check arr[1]=7 → No
Step 3: Check arr[2]=1 → No
Step 4: Check arr[3]=9 → FOUND!
4 steps for 9 elements
Worst case: 9 steps (all elements)
SLOW for large arrays!"]
        
        BINARY["BINARY SEARCH O(log n)
---
Sorted: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
Searching for: 9

Step 1: Check middle = 5 → Too small!
Step 2: Check middle of right = 7 → Too small!
Step 3: Check middle = 8 → Too small!
Step 4: Check 9 → FOUND!
4 steps for 9 elements
Worst case: log₂(9) ≈ 4 steps
VERY FAST! But requires SORTED data"]
    end
    
    ANALOGY["IR Analogy:
Linear = Calling every UN member alphabetically
Binary = Calling the Security Council first,
         then regional groups, then specific countries
         
Which is faster?"]
    
    style LINEAR fill:#ffe6e6,stroke:#cc0000
    style BINARY fill:#e6ffe6,stroke:#00cc00,stroke-width:2px
    style ANALOGY fill:#ffffe6,stroke:#cccc00
